# Minimal inittab for first mainline-boot hardware test on the TrimUI Smart Pro.
# Deliberately skips OpenRC's full service sequence for now — just mounts the
# basics and drops straight to an interactive shell on the UART console, to
# keep this test's moving parts to a minimum. Alpine's real busybox/apk
# userland is still fully present; can layer OpenRC back in once this is
# confirmed working.
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t proc proc /proc
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t sysfs sysfs /sys
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devtmpfs devtmpfs /dev
::sysinit:/bin/mkdir -p /dev/pts
::sysinit:/bin/mount -t devpts devpts /dev/pts
::sysinit:/sbin/watchdog -T 16 -t 5 /dev/watchdog
::sysinit:/etc/audio-defaults.sh
::sysinit:/etc/usb-net.sh
::sysinit:/etc/bt-up.sh
::sysinit:/etc/wake-sources.sh
::sysinit:/bin/echo "=== Alpine minimal boot test — TrimUI Smart Pro mainline port ==="
ttyS0::respawn:/bin/ash
::ctrlaltdel:/sbin/reboot
::shutdown:/bin/umount -a -r
